  "purpose": "The hostile-monitor attempts of anchor's control breach image (M11-8; planning/mvp-m11-plan.md, D-10's control-hart column): HS code on the control hart, hart 0, after its activation and before it reads any ring, attempts each target D-10 names with each kind of access and call, and records each one's trap. g0 and g1 are VS domain 0's and VS domain 1's extents. Each row's at is the physical target; tools/gen-breach.py makes the access's address from it by the row's mode.",
  "trust": "Test data. tools/gen-breach.py checks every row against the control hart's profile and its call list in the hooked image's descriptor (an outcome of denied needs a right the profile lacks, allowed every right it needs; refused a call the list does not hold, rejected and zero a listed console write as the firmware decides it, with the error the row names) and refuses two rows whose written or read bytes meet.",
  "scope": "anchor's breach-c and its -off copy, which makes only the rows with a witness.",
  "role": "control",
